  "assertions": [
    {
      "scenario": "V4 no-dispatch reader exposes only owned recovery operations and preserves UNKNOWN close",
      "checks": [
        "Missing arguments, an extra requestImpl accessor, and a proxy configuration are rejected without getter or proxy-trap execution or owner_epoch advancement.",
        "The valid V4 reader exposes exactly nine frozen recovery operations and no actuating/root/store capability.",
        "Original request, recovery state and whole-catalog keys remain exact; persisted quarantine is PERSISTED_UNKNOWN with NONE authority and false action/delivery flags.",
        "The legacy recovery-plan alias routes to the state-plan path. A detached local plan close is cached.",
        "The actual root cached close Promise rejects XP_CHILD_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN; the owned native store close returns exactly once and its ownership slot is released."
      ]
    },
    {
      "scenario": "V4 reader plans and whole-catalog collection keep declared success powerless",
      "checks": [
        "A reopened V4 reader retains the existing quarantine.",
        "Declared INCLUDED/SUCCEEDED input may project terminal SUCCEEDED and a declared read-only next action, but the owned top-level next action remains RECONCILIATION_REQUIRED with no authority.",
        "A whole-catalog recovery collection has exactly the retained original; an empty catalog input is refused without invalidating the existing collection.",
        "Collection close returns cached DETACHED_HISTORICAL metadata and closes its local child plan once; it does not close the root DB.",
        "The subsequent owned root close again rejects UNKNOWN after the native DB close returns."
      ]
    },
    {
      "scenario": "V4 observation collection latches after root close and retains detached history only",
      "checks": [
        "A V4 observation collection can retain a declared success observation without clearing quarantine or gaining authority.",
        "Closing the actual root first returns the native DB close but leaves the root UNKNOWN.",
        "The first post-root collection snapshot read fails XP_CLOSED; the next is RP_RECOVERY_OBSERVATION_COLLECTION_UNAVAILABLE. There is no live-read retry.",
        "Collection close detaches historical data with LIVE_READ_FAILED and WHOLE_REFRESH_FAILED markers, closes its local children, and returns the same cached metadata on repeated close/getSnapshot.",
        "After detach, observing a valid member is refused CLOSED; an unknown member retains MEMBER_NOT_FOUND precedence. The historical state remains powerless."
      ]
    }
  ],
